  "executive_summary": {
    "finding": "The radiometric transformation distinction between np.log1p(max(DN,0)) and 10*log10(DN+1e-6) is fully reconciled. The early draft design (PHASE_EXP07_P0 draft contract) proposed 10*log10(DN + 1e-6) and colloquially termed it 'pseudo-dB'. However, the formal frozen protocol contract (C4 Section 3 & Section 10, C15, C21) and 100% of executable training runs (Run 001, Run 002, Run 003, C22-B Diag01, C22-D Replication) implemented and executed np.log1p(np.maximum(raw_dn, 0.0)) with standardized TRAIN-only normalization. Calling log1p 'pseudo-dB' in historical reports was a loose documentation terminology error. Calibrated physical sigma0 dB was never established.",
    "mathematical_equivalence_status": "NOT_EQUIVALENT",
    "mathematical_note": "np.log1p(x) is natural logarithm ln(1+x), whereas 10*log10(x) is (10/ln(10))*ln(x) \u2248 4.3429*ln(x). They differ by a scale factor of ~4.34 and offset. However, subsequent standardization (z - mu)/sigma absorbs linear scale and shift, so both map linear inputs to standardized normal-like ranges, though they are mathematically distinct functions.",
    "executed_representation_across_all_runs": "AGGREGATED_RAW_DN_LOG1P_STANDARDIZED",
    "calibration_status": "EXPLICITLY_UNCALIBRATED (detected amplitude DN, not physical sigma0/gamma0)"
  },
